    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_5f8563b04db8719671ac8c21c259a57222d9a2bb08dc479502ab64c15f7ee394",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The effective small-degree result divides an infinite verification problem at a computable threshold: saddle-point asymptotics control normalized Jensen coefficient vectors inside a hyperbolicity-preserving neighborhood of H_d beyond the threshold, while Hermite's criterion checks every earlier shift. The coefficient tables provide a visible diagnostic of the normalization's approach to the same Hermite target but are not part of the certificate.",
