    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_948156433b4ea5696e9355afba8d3ea95c84609dc2c4bdd1c8443b109a8e7329",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Polya's all-degree, all-shift Jensen criterion turns the completed zeta zero problem into finite coefficient-window tests, while the Hermite-limit theorem and the saddle-derived ratio expansion show that each fixed degree eventually enters a stable real-rooted regime. Together these units locate both the finite algebraic shadow of RH and the asymptotic mechanism that controls its large-shift tail.",
